<%# Compact Show/Hide toggle sitting beside a section heading (see
    events/_section_heading). It's a second control for the same panel as the top
    toggle bar; panel-toggle keeps every control for a panel in sync, so both
    labels flip together.

    The visible text is just "Show"/"Hide" — the heading next to it supplies the
    subject — so `section` names it for screen readers, where the heading isn't
    adjacent. aria-expanded carries the state, so that label stays static.

    Locals:
      name:    the data-panel-toggle-name of the panel it toggles
      section: the section's name, for the accessible label ("Toggle breakdowns")
      open:    whether the panel is open on this render. Default false. %>
<% open = local_assigns.fetch(:open, false) %>
<button type="button"
        data-panel-toggle-target="button"
        data-panel-toggle-name="<%= name %>"
        data-panel-toggle-shown-label="Hide"
        data-panel-toggle-hidden-label="Show"
        data-action="panel-toggle#toggle"
        aria-expanded="<%= open %>"
        aria-label="Toggle <%= section %>"
        class="shrink-0 rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600 hover:bg-gray-50 hover:text-gray-800 print:hidden">
  <span data-panel-toggle-target="label"><%= open ? "Hide" : "Show" %></span>
</button>
